CloudBurrow patch 10 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1205).

The bug: datasets.patch and datasets.update changed the dataset the
request had read (Dataset.UpdateContentIfExists, Dataset.UpdateContent)
and answered it, but never wrote it to the metadata store, which every
request reads its project and datasets from: a datasets.get afterwards
read the dataset as it was before (measured, #1200).

The patch writes the changed metadata with Repository.UpdateDataset, in
a transaction as datasets.delete makes one, through a new Dataset.Save.
What a patch merges and an update replaces is unchanged here: CloudBurrow's
front sends both methods as a datasets.update of the whole dataset, merged
as BigQuery merges a patch (internal/bigqueryfront/datasetupdate.go).

